st usable poll is 51 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District is an even partisan split, and first-term Republican Tom Barrett is defending the seat against Democrat William Lawrence in what raters call one of the closest House races of 2026. Five of ten expert ratings call it a tossup, while the rest lean Democratic for a flip, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at roughly 56 to 58 percent.\n\nBarrett holds a large fundraising lead, but outside groups have spent heavily against him, and recent coverage highlights attacks on his healthcare record and his break with Trump on a war issue. The only recent poll, from August, shows Lawrence up two. A strong Democratic midterm environment gives Lawrence the slight edge, though the race remains genuinely competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}]}